# Portfolio repository rules

> The definitive rules live in [`AGENTS.md`](mdc:AGENTS.md). This file is a
> Cursor-shaped summary that Cursor will always inject into context.

## Identity

This is **Ayush Yadav's** proprietary personal portfolio (see `LICENSE`).
Do not invent professional history, customers, or metrics. The only
authoritative source for those facts is `src/content/*.ts`.

## Stack

Next.js 16 App Router · React 19 · TypeScript 6 strict (`noUncheckedIndexedAccess`) ·
Tailwind CSS 4 · next-intl 4 · Vitest · Playwright · Zod 4 · Resend · framer-motion.

## i18n — the load-bearing decision

`src/i18n/routing.ts` uses `localePrefix: "never"`. **Every page lives at the
same URL across all six locales.** Switching language updates the
`NEXT_LOCALE` cookie + re-renders server components without touching the URL.
Never reintroduce `/hi/...` / `/ja/...` style prefixes.

Always import from `@/i18n/navigation`, not from `next/link` /
`next/navigation`, for internal routes.

Every server `page.tsx`:

```tsx
import { setRequestLocale, getTranslations } from "next-intl/server";

export default async function Page({ params }: { params: Promise<{ locale: string }> }) {
  const { locale } = await params;
  setRequestLocale(locale);
  const t = await getTranslations("namespace");
  // ...
}
```

## Coding non-negotiables

- Server components by default; `"use client"` only when interactivity demands it.
- No raw `<img>` except in `src/components/experience/company-logo.tsx`.
- No new `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` (the only existing use is the Person JSON-LD).
- All animations must gate on `useReducedMotion()` from `framer-motion`.
- All user-visible strings come from `messages/en.json` via `t()`.
- External `<a>` links use `target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
- Tailwind tokens: `text-fg`, `bg-bg-elev`, `text-accent-cyan`, etc. — never raw hex.

## Quality gate

```sh
npm run format && npm run lint && npm run lint:md && \
  npm run typecheck && npm test -- --run && npm run build
```

CI runs the same gate plus Playwright e2e, axe accessibility, CodeQL,
dependency-review, and `npm audit`. `--max-warnings=0` everywhere — zero
warnings tolerated.

## Commit messages

Conventional Commits: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`,
`test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`, `deps`. Subject ≤ 100 chars.

## Where to look first

- `src/content/*.ts` — the truth about projects, experience, skills, metrics.
- `messages/en.json` — every translatable string.
- `src/app/[locale]/` — routes and layouts.
- `src/components/` — UI, grouped by feature folder.
- `src/lib/` — pure utilities; this is also where coverage thresholds bite.
- `docs/ADR/` — past architecture decisions; read before contradicting them.
